# Meeting minutes template of a housing co-operative: the document documents/examples/general-meeting with Slots for
# each general meeting. The co-operative, the layout, the labels of the meeting details and the signature blocks are
# part of the template; the date and times of the meeting, the subject, the place, the chair and the secretary (who
# takes the minutes and signs them), the attendance and the quorum, the minutes and their footnotes come in the data.
# The minutes are one Markdown, with numbered headings (Numbered in the rules of Heading 2 and Heading 3), lists with
# their own markers per level (Bullet markers, Number markers), and block quotes and rules that the engine styles with
# the For element rules of Block quote and Divider; the footnotes it calls ([^id]) are objects with their Id and text.
# The meeting details are a Grid of labels and values above it, and the signatures a Stack kept together. The stamp is a
# Page overlay rotated 8 degrees that appears only on the first page (Pages: first); it is optional, and without it in
# the data the minutes come out unstamped. general-meeting.json has the sample data.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: Letter
		Margin: 54 72 62 72
	Title: Minutes of the general meeting of ${date} · Linden Street Housing Co-operative
	Subject: <subject>
	Author: Linden Street Housing Co-operative
	Language: en-US
	Page overlay: {?stamp}
		Id: stamp
		Pages: first
		Offset: -30 -20 auto auto
		Rotate: 8
		Layer: 2
		Text: <text>
			Style: stamp
	Page overlay:
		Id: footer
		Offset: auto 0 -40 0
		Style: footer
		Stack:
			Horizontal: justify
			Item:
				Text: Linden Street Housing Co-operative · General meeting, ${date}
			Item:
				Text: Page {page} of {pages}
	Section:
		Text: Linden Street Housing Co-operative
			Style: org
		Heading 1:
			Text: Minutes of the general meeting
		Grid:
			Id: details
			Style: details
			Area:
				Text: Date
					Style: detail-label
			Area:
				Text: ${weekday} ${date}, ${start} to ${end}
			Area:
				Text: Place
					Style: detail-label
			Area:
				Text: <place>
			Area:
				Text: Chair
					Style: detail-label
			Area:
				Text: <chair>
			Area:
				Text: Minutes
					Style: detail-label
			Area:
				Text: ${secretary}, secretary
			Area:
				Text: Present
					Style: detail-label
			Area:
				Text: ${present} of ${households} member households, so the meeting was quorate (the quorum is ${quorum})
		Markdown:
			Id: minutes
			Style: minutes
			Content >>
				<minutes>
		Footnote: [footnotes]
			Id: <id>
			Paragraph: <text>
		Stack:
			Id: signatures
			Style: signatures
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Block:
					Style: signature
					Text: ${chair}, chair
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Block:
					Style: signature
					Text: ${secretary}, secretary
